# Architecture & Backend Rules

When modifying data structures, Supabase client services, or application contracts:

## 1. Database & Schema Modeling (`database-design`)

- Always declare strict TypeScript types in `types/` for all Supabase table rows and payloads.
- Ensure foreign keys, unique constraints (e.g. canonical URLs), and indexes for queried columns (`user_id`, `clean_url`, `created_at`).
- Keep Row Level Security (RLS) policies in mind for user-scoped data.

## 2. Decision Records (`architecture-decision-records`)

- Document high-impact architectural changes (e.g. AI engine integrations, caching layers, native bridges) in `docs/adr/`.
- Structure: Status, Context, Decision, Consequences.

## 3. Persistent Knowledge (`saving-workspace-context`)

- Store long-term knowledge, research findings, and API specifications in workspace documentation so context is preserved across AI sessions.
